{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310699,"nonce":"6uqbZPz5BrorcVoYsnm38SDcVDo=","title":"Tests that PASS by exit code but print garbage — surfaces real runtime bugs in RTTI, interface cast, Channel, exception stack","message":"`run_haxe_tests.sh` only checks process exit status. Tests that print wrong values without throwing still \"pass\". Audit on 2026-05-24 of the 128/128 suite found four real runtime bugs hidden this way.\n\n\n**Expected vs actual (lines 1049–1063 of test_results.txt):**\n\n| stmt | expected | actual |\n|---|---|---|\n| `var d:Animal = new Dog(...); d is Animal` | true | true |\n| `d is Dog` | true | **false** |\n| `var c = new Cat(...); c is Animal` | true | **false** |\n| `Std.isOfType(d, Dog)` | true | **false** |\n\nLikely cause: `is` is doing TypeId equality on the static type instead of walking the runtime class hierarchy from the object header. The header type_id is correct (we know Type.getClass works) but the inheritance walk is missing or only fires for one direction.\n\n\n**Expected vs actual (lines 795–799):**\n\n```\ndraw:box           →   draw:           (name field empty after interface dispatch)\nnull               →   null            ✓\nclick:submit       →   click:          (same — name field empty)\nbutton-draw:submit →   fail4           (cast(btn, IDrawable) returned null; Button inherits IDrawable from Widget)\n```\n\nTwo distinct bugs:\n1. **Field empty**: After interface fat-pointer dispatch, `name` field reads as \"\" or null. Likely fat-ptr object pointer wrong, or interface method dispatches with wrong `this`.\n2. **Inherited interface cast fails**: `cast(btn, IDrawable)` should succeed because `Button extends Widget` and `Widget implements IDrawable`. Cast checks only direct implementation, doesn't walk parent chain.\n\nBoth touch the interface dispatch / vtable code recently modified in commit `a86d8a9`.\n\n\n```\ntrace(sum); // sum of 0+10+20+30+40 = 100\n```\n\nActual: `513119280` (random heap word). Channel send/receive over Thread.spawn corrupts. Real bug.\n\n\nDebug-mode preset should populate stack via debug-mode guarded_call (per [[bugs-cleanup-scopes-frees-captures]]). The `details.indexOf(\"Called from\") \u003e= 0` returns false. Either capture is disabled or details() doesn't include frames.\n\n\nWhen fixing these, add an explicit `assert(actual == expected)` in the test source so PASS truly means \"behaviour correct\" — exit-code-only checks make these regressions invisible. The runner could also be extended to diff against `// Expected:` comments where present.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_silent_garbage_pass` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}